Limit: a pending create with no response that finds a same-named repository without its marker is refused as indeterminate; the marker lives in the public repository description, so an edited description turns an adoptable repository into that refusal
Ruled-out: executing an executable plan the caller supplies, checked by the PLAN digest and operation identities | those said nothing about desired state, so a weaker protection executed under an unchanged approval; the PLAN artifact's own operations are executed instead
Ruled-out: adopting a same-named repository after a lost create by its name | indistinguishable from someone else's; adoption needs the node id the create response named or the marker the create recorded, and otherwise it is refused
Ruled-out: removing a leftover checkout of the same bootstrap operation automatically | a live run of the operation cannot be told from a dead one, so the checkout is named in the refusal and left for a person
Warn: plan_submit still accepts operation identities only, so a PLAN submitted over MCP is refused as not executable until it carries each operation's desired state
Warn: the REST half and git must address the same host: every gh api call names github.com and the gh child drops GH_HOST
