Limit: a checkout left by a run that died, or one still running, is refused by name until a person removes it; only then does the operation resume from the GitHub ledger
Ruled-out: reclaiming a leftover checkout of this operation when its ledger is complete and its HEAD is the receipted push | a matching HEAD does not make tracked edits, untracked or ignored files recoverable, and two retries could each delete what the other just claimed; every leftover checkout is refused by name and kept
Ruled-out: keeping the produced result in a file beside the ledger for the runner to activate on retry | a copy only the producer can vouch for can be forged by anyone who can write the file, and the runner activated it before admitting the approval; the caller's store keeps it inside the producer's cleanup
